the-firm-as-one-program-77 : Pull
the-firm-as-one-program-77 = pull the-firm-as-one-program-source (whole the-firm-as-one-program-source) (cons (span #30953 #31518) nil) (restated (unlines (cons "- **S1** The gains multiply instead of adding, which changes the rate of learning of a firm built as one program (all of the outline's “Value to the firm”)." (cons "  The lines of value to the firm do not add; they multiply. Faster iteration means more strategies tested, cumulative knowledge means each test builds on all earlier ones, proven risk means more capital behind each, and exact reasoning under uncertainty means better decisions per unit of capital. Artificial researchers multiply all of it again. The result is a firm whose rate of learning is itself rising. Its advantage over competitors is a difference in kind, not a margin." nil)))) as-written
the-firm-as-one-program-78 : Pull
the-firm-as-one-program-78 = pull the-firm-as-one-program-source (whole the-firm-as-one-program-source) (cons (span #31518 #32067) nil) (restated (unlines (cons "- **S2** The market concentrates toward the firm built as one program in hyperactivity ([S1: The gains multiply instead of adding, which changes the firm's rate of learning (all of layer 3)])." (cons "  Electronic trading is close to a zero-sum contest between firms over the same flow, and market share already concentrates toward the firms with the best technology. A discontinuity in technology produces a discontinuity in concentration: the firm built as one program takes opportunities first, correctly, at full size, everywhere, and its competitors trade against a counterparty that is better informed and quicker to adapt. That is why a figure of several billion understates it." nil)))) as-written
the-firm-as-one-program-79 : Pull
the-firm-as-one-program-79 = pull the-firm-as-one-program-source (whole the-firm-as-one-program-source) (cons (span #32067 #32513) nil) (restated (unlines (cons "- **S3** Prices converge on what is true, so the edge that profits came from shrinks ([S2: The market concentrates toward the firm that has this ([S1])])." (cons "  Edge in markets is information not yet reflected in prices. As the firm built as one program extracts it, prices become correct sooner, and the edge available to everyone shrinks. The firm profits precisely by removing the ignorance that made profit possible. Profit in trading measures collective ignorance, and this system dispels collective ignorance at machine speed." nil)))) as-written
the-firm-as-one-program-80 : Pull
the-firm-as-one-program-80 = pull the-firm-as-one-program-source (whole the-firm-as-one-program-source) (cons (span #32513 #33611) nil) (restated (unlines (cons "- **S4** What Hayek argued prices must carry becomes directly available, so prices stop being the main way the economy coordinates ([S3: Prices converge on what is true, so the edge that profits came from shrinks ([S2])], [P9: Content-addressed, decentralized exchange of code with its proofs (hyperactivity v31 §10.8)])." (cons "  Hayek argued in 1945 that no central planner could hold the knowledge dispersed across a society, so prices had to carry it in compressed form. Hyperactivity is not a central planner: it has no canonical state, every participant holds its own, and constructions are exchanged between peers. But the knowledge that prices compress becomes available directly, with its evidence, to every participant. Once that holds, prices stop being the primary carrier of coordination, and an economy built around competing partial knowledge gives way to one built around shared knowledge. The trading firm is where this starts, because no institution has more money riding on the gap between what prices know and what is true. The same mechanism, aimed at knowledge instead of money, is the dispelling of ignorance across the human superorganism: thousands of minds in one firm becoming one reasoning process is the small case of billions of minds doing the same." nil)))) as-written
the-firm-as-one-program-81 : Pull
the-firm-as-one-program-81 = pull the-firm-as-one-program-source (whole the-firm-as-one-program-source) (cons (span #33611 #33621) nil) as-written as-written
the-firm-as-one-program-82 : Pull
the-firm-as-one-program-82 = pull the-firm-as-one-program-source (whole the-firm-as-one-program-source) (cons (span #33621 #33831) nil) (restated (unlines (cons "- **N1** Of the outline “The Firm as One Program”, two points carry the most weight." (cons "  C10 (AI researchers at any scale, because their output is checked, not trusted ([P11])) is the largest multiplier: checked construction lets AI research scale without trust. S1 (The gains multiply instead of adding, which changes the firm's rate of learning (all of layer 3)) is what turns a list of savings into a change in kind. See [C10: AI researchers at any scale, because their output is checked, not trusted ([P11])], [S1: The gains multiply instead of adding, which changes the firm's rate of learning (all of layer 3)]." nil)))) as-written
the-firm-as-one-program-83 : Pull
the-firm-as-one-program-83 = pull the-firm-as-one-program-source (whole the-firm-as-one-program-source) (cons (span #33831 #34463) nil) (restated (unlines (cons "- **N2** The bridge to the rationality claim." (cons (quoted (cons "  P1 (Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (§1, §10.4))'s warrant is the formal form of " (cons "the rational actor cannot be incorrect" (cons ", and that is what C17 (Disagreements resolve on a presented shared basis ([P1], plus common ground)) runs on. A rational actor concludes P only when it holds a construction of P over every history compatible with what it observed. Where no such construction exists it concludes nothing, so it is never wrong. The language therefore marks exactly what is amenable to rule-based logic: what is derived, what is observed, and what is a stated premise. English could always carry perfect inference for the rational; the language makes that discipline executable and shared. See [P1: Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (hyperactivity v31 §1, §10.4)], [C17: Disagreements resolve on a presented shared basis ([P1], plus common ground)]." nil)))) nil)))) as-written
